{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788047941031081002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"dialectal-acidotic-coati","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"130240252f83bea5dfbb7181891e15f3646bb821b5f967abef34e85f1336d278","event_uuid":"da3fe3ad-c39f-4773-b4b5-2c99abb69d6a","position":{"commit_sha":"c288fb519d1ee548c6b7cd9d49b1447a39d866e4","position":"1788047040346318001-da3fe3ad-c39f-4773-b4b5-2c99abb69d6a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c2ffd86978c3de17f5112bf2ddcf27a6c11fa1038e6c49bd89d6a8e92a95ae09","event_uuid":"f70123fc-d3f5-44cf-9ec7-7c715c91e902","position":{"commit_sha":"262fcad26878d2dfe2ee3c9342c4aa0d1baa7ed0","position":"1788047060940218001-f70123fc-d3f5-44cf-9ec7-7c715c91e902"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"84928329b444f6ba001dd51c2a166dfc16482608cac6c59a3cd3c3a0cb4e1914","event_uuid":"070fcf5f-d338-4fd2-a9fe-9b6ade073424","position":{"commit_sha":"75f82b82199d659e35144df11c9be7b130c95dc1","position":"1788047884977946001-070fcf5f-d338-4fd2-a9fe-9b6ade073424"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c223873c20ff34285e7b23b7de5865b48716d95f107f86d7eddbef3dfc49d32c","event_uuid":"3e93e944-6a7a-4fcc-8f0b-7e07e9b383c0","position":{"commit_sha":"02cb50de6af1ebde1ea2da798b53719e9015f310","position":"1788047941031081001-3e93e944-6a7a-4fcc-8f0b-7e07e9b383c0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788047040346318001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nCut the next fix release, 0.13.1, from reviewed main using docs/releasing.md. Prior\npackage/tag: 0.13.0/v0.13.0 (currently live on PyPI and the latest GitHub Release). Only\n6 commits landed on main since v0.13.0, all internal/non-user-facing (config/plan_review\nsplit, SSM secret handling, MCP registry description-length fix, LLM cache/enrichment\ntweaks) -- CHANGELOG.md's [Unreleased] section on origin/main is empty, so step 1a is a\nno-op retitle/placeholder rather than a curated entry. PyPI is immutable; publication uses\nthe dispatch-from-main workflow and its pypi environment approval.\n\nKnown risk: ticket hyperbolic-pernicious-drongo (0.13.0) closed FAILED because, after PyPI\npublish succeeded in one release.yml run, the mcp_registry job failed (server.json\ndescription length); by the time the fix landed, PyPI 0.13.0 was immutable so the workflow\ncould not be re-dispatched (400 File already exists), and the documented manual\nmcp-publisher fallback was blocked by a navapbc org OAuth-App access restriction needing\norg-admin action. The registry still reports 0.12.0 as isLatest. Mitigation: before\ndispatch, confirm that OAuth-App restriction is resolved so the manual fallback is usable if\nmcp_registry fails again post-publish. If it still cannot be made to report 0.13.1 after\nexhausting both paths, close with that one AC marked [non-codebase, known-blocked] plus a\nlinked follow-up ticket, rather than yanking the already-live PyPI/GitHub Release for a\nregistry-only gap.\n\n## Plan\n- Fresh worktree from origin/main; confirm prerequisites, identity, Gerrit rights, channel\n  state, and the navapbc OAuth-App access posture (mitigation above).\n- Bump pyproject.toml + every server.json version to 0.13.1; regenerate uv.lock; add a\n  0.13.1 CHANGELOG section (today's date) via the changelog generator as a starting point,\n  hand-curated, with a fresh empty Unreleased section and updated compare links.\n- Regenerate tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json (__version__ bump), the step the 0.13.0\n  release ticket documented as newly required.\n- Preflight: version-lockstep guard, release-specific tests, lint, typecheck, full test\n  suite, build, and twine check of the artifacts.\n- Commit with DCO + Change-Id + rebar-ticket trailer; push to Gerrit; earn LLM-Review +1 and\n  Verified +1 with no unresolved comments; Submit.\n- Dispatch release.yml from main with version=0.13.1; approve the pypi environment\n  deployment; monitor to completion, watching mcp_registry given the prior failure there.\n- Verify PyPI + PEP 740 provenance, GitHub tag/release + artifacts, MCP Registry (confirm\n  0.13.1 isLatest), and the Homebrew tap bump.\n- Channel-install nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.1 and run the packaged post-publication probe.\n- Record receipts; close only once all acceptance criteria are met (or the one documented\n  registry exception above applies).\n\n## File impact\n- pyproject.toml -- package version bump\n- server.json -- MCP manifest/package version bump\n- uv.lock -- root package version lockstep with pyproject.toml\n- CHANGELOG.md -- new 0.13.1 release section and compare links\n- tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json -- __version__ bump\n\n## Rollback / failure policy\nBefore publish: stop on any failed guard/review/CI vote; remediate via a new Gerrit\npatchset. After publish, PyPI cannot be replaced: yank 0.13.1, de-list its GitHub Release,\nand cut a fixed next patch version; never overwrite artifacts or retag published content.\nIf PyPI/GitHub Release publish succeeds but mcp_registry fails and the manual fallback is\nalso blocked (the exact 0.13.0 failure mode): do not yank the already-live PyPI/GitHub\nRelease artifacts for this reason alone; record the gap as a documented, linked follow-up\nand mark the corresponding acceptance criterion [non-codebase, known-blocked] rather than\nleaving the ticket in limbo.\n\n## Testing\n- Run the version-lockstep release guard script against pyproject.toml and server.json with\n  version 0.13.1 and confirm it exits 0.\n- Run \"make lint\", \"make typecheck\", and \"make test\" under the worktree virtualenv and\n  confirm each exits 0.\n- Run \"python -m build\" to produce the 0.13.1 wheel and sdist, then \"python -m twine check\"\n  against the built artifacts and confirm it exits 0.\n- Run the pypi-attestations verifier against the published 0.13.1 wheel, scoped to the\n  navapbc/rebar repository, and confirm it exits 0.\n- Install the channel-published nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.1 build and run the packaged\n  scripts/probe_rebar.py probe against it, confirming zero failures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] pyproject.toml declares version 0.13.1.\n- [ ] server.json top-level version is 0.13.1.\n- [ ] Every server.json packages[].version is 0.13.1.\n- [ ] uv.lock records the root nava-rebar package at version 0.13.1.\n- [ ] Running \"uv lock --check\" exits 0.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md contains a 0.13.1 section dated with today's release date.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG.md has a fresh Unreleased section and correct 0.13.1 compare links.\n- [ ] tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json reflects __version__ 0.13.1.\n- [ ] The release_guards.py version-lockstep check exits 0 for version 0.13.1 against\n      pyproject.toml and server.json.\n- [ ] The release-specific guard and workflow pin unit tests\n      (tests/unit/test_release_guards.py and tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py) all pass.\n- [ ] \"make lint\" exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] \"make typecheck\" exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] \"make test\" exits 0 under the worktree virtualenv.\n- [ ] \"python -m build\" produces the 0.13.1 wheel and sdist.\n- [ ] \"python -m twine check\" exits 0 for the built artifacts.\n- [ ] The release commit contains DCO sign-off, a Gerrit Change-Id, and this rebar-ticket\n      trailer.\n- [ ] Gerrit records LLM-Review +1 on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit records Verified +1 on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit has no unresolved comments on the release change.\n- [ ] Gerrit submits the release change and the resulting commit is on main.\n- [ ] release.yml is dispatched from main with version input 0.13.1.\n- [ ] The required pypi environment deployment is approved.\n- [ ] Every required release.yml job completes successfully (build, wheel_test, sdist_test,\n      publish, mcp_verify, mcp_registry, github_release).\n- [ ] PyPI serves nava-rebar 0.13.1.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The pypi-attestations verifier passes against the published 0.13.1\n      wheel scoped to the navapbc/rebar repository.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] GitHub tag v0.13.1 resolves to the released main commit.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] GitHub Release v0.13.1 is marked Latest and attaches the 0.13.1 wheel\n      and sdist.\n- [ ] [non-codebase, known-blocked-risk] MCP Registry reports io.github.navapbc/rebar\n      version 0.13.1 as isLatest, or (if blocked by the known OAuth-App restriction even\n      after the mitigation above) a linked follow-up ticket documents the gap and this item\n      is explicitly marked as the accepted exception.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] Homebrew tap Formula/rebar.rb points to the 0.13.1 PyPI sdist URL with\n      matching SHA-256 (or the scheduled autobump run is confirmed to have picked it up).\n- [ ] A fresh channel install of nava-rebar[mcp]==0.13.1 passes scripts/probe_rebar.py with\n      zero failures.\n- [ ] Release receipts, any exceptions, and the rollback disposition are recorded on this\n      ticket.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"package version bump"},{"path":"server.json","reason":"MCP manifest/package version bump"},{"path":"uv.lock","reason":"root package version lockstep"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"new 0.13.1 release section and compare links"},{"path":"tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json","reason":"__version__ bump"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"334d-71ba-589f-4eea","ticket_type":"task","title":"Release rebar 0.13.1","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["da3fe3ad-c39f-4773-b4b5-2c99abb69d6a","f70123fc-d3f5-44cf-9ec7-7c715c91e902","070fcf5f-d338-4fd2-a9fe-9b6ade073424","3e93e944-6a7a-4fcc-8f0b-7e07e9b383c0"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788047941031081002,"uuid":"971e3e16-4e11-4cba-b4ca-191c07807505"}